  "notes": "Single-staff melody with two stacked verses. Verse 1 has one syllable fewer than verse 2 in line 3 (\"trem-_-bling\" vs \"bow down their heads\"): bar 6 beat 3 (c''8) carries a verse-2 syllable (\"their\") but NO verse-1 syllable. The final melisma \"pass-ing _\" is slurred in both verses. DAMAGE (stain-pencil): Rehearsal copy: coffee ring stains (scan: one ring over the music), graphite pencil marks - circled notes, handwritten words (\"rit.\", \"breathe\", \"p\", \"cresc.\" ...), breath ticks/commas, arrows, phrase arcs. Severe adds three stains, yellow and pink highlighter over staff passages, blue ballpoint circles/words and margin scribbles. Exact positions of every mark are listed per file in meta.annotations. TRUTH LIMITATIONS: Handwritten marks (including handwritten dynamics such as \"p\", \"mf\", \"cresc.\", \"rit.\" and fingerings) are NOT in the truth: the truth only contains the engraved music. A conversion that adds them as dynamics/words/fingerings is wrong for scoring purposes."
